WEBVTT

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.870
That's tragic, isn't it?

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:14.450
The interstellar ship of the treaty compliance
agency was found in the Deneb System.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.100
The hull was heavily damaged
and there were no survivors.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.750
But there was some fascinating data in the recovered records.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.920
This is?!

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.250
What did Sam Taylor say?

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.840
About that...

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.290
unfortunately the voice data
was badly damaged.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.420
However...

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.850
A self-repairing crystal film
forming an airtight layer...

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:43.770
Yes. That, and the girl is
controlling the Orichalt.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:48.860
He may be a half-baked experiment,
but Sam did a good job.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.240
This girl...

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.110
Is she that "Orillian" proposed by Arisugawa?

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:59.240
I think we can be sure of that.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:51.950
Now I can understand that what doctor
Arisugawa theorized was true....

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:57.140
Orichalt being a message spread by an unknown civilization

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:59.280
in an attempt to contact other civilizations...

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.030
was completely wrong.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:06.900
This ore was a hindrance to that civilization,
it was garbage and an obstacle...

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:13.810
The wandering planet, Rajeev, is likely a device
they made to collect the hazardous Orichalt.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.260
We were collected as a piece of that garbage...

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.180
Wah!

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.220
And at this point cannot hope to escape.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.390
Humanity touched something
that was not be touched.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.170
It's just as doctor Arisugawa predicted...

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.660
Doctor Arisugawa...

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.690
This is the voice data of the ship
log salvaged by Maya and me

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:38.330
from the manned probe,
recovered by Stulti's systems.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:45.130
As you just heard, the wandering planets are an Orichalt
collection device constructed by an unknown civilization.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:47.920
We can probably assume them
to be fully automatic.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.010
Question.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.550
What is this "unknown civilization" anyway?

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:53.340
Do you know, Maya?

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:58.260
No, there were no theories like that about Orichalt at the Academy.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:02.600
Same for the army. So that means the information was kept secret?

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.950
That's scary!

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.400
So where are those unknown guys now?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.080
It doesn't seem like the planets have any
other goals after collecting Orichalt.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.240
We should probably assume
they're extinct by now.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.050
Kicked the bucket, huh?
What a troublesome civilization.

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.410
Geh! Communication failure.
I'm sorry.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.120
So this wandering planet, Rajeev?

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.370
Why is it going after Alice?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:31.310
The crystal film forming the airtight layer
around Alice constantly emits Orichalt.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.420
That must have attracted it.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:38.730
The minute the Observer ship released the Orichalt for a jump,

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.380
those things started aiming there instead.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.050
That's evidence that they were
attracted by a larger Orichalt.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.410
Did the federation know about that?

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:50.600
Politically speaking, they had no
choice but to hide it.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.450
If Orichalt became unusable, that would
cut the lifeline of colonized planets.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.820
I mean, there's a chance it
could destroy humanity.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:03.270
That said, if it keeps being used, the wandering planets
will eventually come and lay waste to everything.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.920
No matter where you turn, it's a dead end.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.250
Then we must ring all alarm bells
and warn all of humanity!

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.610
That's a grandiose thought.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:14.640
Consider your position first!

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.800
You're still a criminal who was
selling Academy's data!

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:22.300
And now that you've came across
classified information,

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.890
they'll catch and dispose of you!

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.980
Am I right, Lieutenant?

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:27.980
Most likely.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:31.940
And that goes for all of us, right?
What do we do?

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:35.260
The choices we can make right now...

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.110
There are only two.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.680
Surrender and let the federation catch us.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:44.750
Or escape somewhere far enough neither
them nor the planets will follow.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:52.380
With so many major criminals, Evertancers, here, it doesn't matter what we're arrested for.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.960
Though it's probably not
the case for Lt. Amanza.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.510
I was opposing Observer.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.510
I'm in the same boat as you.

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:00.890
So shall we run?

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:01.940
Don't be kidding.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:05.380
Anything but primitive self-sufficient life.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:09.890
No movies or shopping, to be honest it sounds quite harsh.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:11.340
Mr. Ido-

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:12.440
Ido, what's your take?

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:17.030
I want to select a third choice.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.910
Doctor Arisugawa.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:22.790
Find out about the person in the ship log.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:27.620
There's nothing in the federation's
database, but what he theorized...

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:32.280
Finding that is the only way to learn more about the connection between

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.880
Orichalt and Rajeev, and about Alice.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.970
So we steal the federation's most
guarded secret, what then?

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:42.450
Find out how to deal with Rajeev
and use that to make a deal.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.850
We'll exchange that information
for our safety.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:51.740
Whew! So guarantee our safety, learn your
past and ensure safe mining of Orichalt?

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.770
Yay, the winner takes it all! I'm in, Ido!

00:06:55.770 --> 00:07:00.860
The fastest way to steal top secret info would
be through a military data relay satellite.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:04.410
If it goes well, we may even
find out who framed us!

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.500
And we can even save humanity!

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.250
Uh...

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.790
Maybe? One day perhaps?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.340
Yeah, we will, we will!
We'll save humanity!

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:22.010
Maya the savior.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:24.490
Your name will be carved
in federation history!

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:25.850
They'll build a bronze statue.

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:28.640
Let's get an autograph while we can!

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:31.770
Why are you making fun of me,
come on!

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:38.900
Confirmed target planet's mass, gravitational constant and penetration velocity.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:43.820
All clear of abnormalities in the penetration depth and obstacles for the swing-by.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.870
Maya, after calculating the point
of gravitational collision

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:49.750
please re-confirm the relative velocity
and trajectory of the ship.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:50.880
Yeah.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:58.310
To avoid pursuit from the wandering planet we
refrained from using Orichalt as much as possible,

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:02.670
even using the ancient navigation techniques,
as we were making our way to the Miguel Net.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:07.600
We sealed most of the Orichalt on the
ship in the containment device,

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:11.730
and even had Alice live in a room
with the same mechanism.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:19.980
Until reaching the Miguel Net it was a long period of boredom called "rest".

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:26.360
Without any information from the federation,
we didn't know how the world changed,

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:30.580
or if it didn't, as two months have passed.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:36.910
These were peaceful days without encountering the army, Observer, or Rajeev.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.080
However, that was...

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:40.420
5...

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:41.550
4...

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:42.550
3...

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:43.500
2...

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.720
1...

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:48.580
We did it!

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:50.600
I'm amazing! I've done it!

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.890
We're finally back inside the
Miguel Net, aren't we?

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:56.310
Aah, it's so great to have information!

00:08:56.310 --> 00:09:00.970
Karla, is there anything about us
or the wandering planet?

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.650
Nope, doesn't look like it.

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:04.690
Anything about the Observer ship?

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.490
Can you also look for anything
about the ship I was on?

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:10.530
Wanna look? Though there doesn't
seem to be any hits for either.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.850
So they're controlling the
information after all.

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:14.450
No way!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:19.470
Mein Ferrande? That incompetent signed a first driver contract with Randell?!

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:23.550
Don't do that! it's gonna put a dent
on my outstanding career!

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:25.660
That's what's bothering you?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.550
Of course my horse!

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:32.140
Stop talking nonsense, save the essential data and cut the link!

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:34.180
Don't forget the federation's
eyes are on us!

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:35.520
Got it, Papa.

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:36.850
Roger that.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:39.030
Jeez, we don't have time for fun.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:42.810
We'll have a briefing in the expanded space!
Gotta decide our next move.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.960
Having fun is a go-go-go!

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:52.670
Let's celebrate the return of our head office, our mothership Stulti, to the Miguel Net with a toast!

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:53.780
Cheers!

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.410
Cheers!

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:58.460
I said it's a briefing.

00:09:58.460 --> 00:09:59.630
Change!

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:03.650
W-What's this scenery data?

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.670
It's a 20th century school.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:09.300
Karla. Anything of interest
in the acquired data?

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:13.280
None at all. In fact, that's
what's interesting.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:17.720
Like you expected, public information is being regulated by the federation.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.310
Which means...

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:24.270
we've got no choice but to salvage the classified
information from a data relay satellite.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.340
It's Karla's time to shine.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.110
I'll certainly do my best.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.030
I've got a question to Grayman and Amanza.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:30.650
Huh?

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:36.410
If you were the mastermind behind these
incidents, how would you catch us?

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.420
Let's see...

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:43.340
Assuming the mastermind found the
heavily damaged Observer's ship,

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:48.210
if it was me I'd dispatch a fleet to the
nearest Miguel Net region.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.340
That, and...

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:52.090
Take our relatives hostage, perhaps.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:54.710
Does anyone here have living relatives?

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:56.700
Hmph.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.130
That's good then.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.270
How about you?

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:04.270
Do you have family?

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:05.940
You think I'd join the military if I did?

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:09.090
Listen up, everyone.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:14.070
This is our only way to strike back at the federation that deceived us.

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:16.080
We are excavators.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:19.460
Be it Orichalt or information,
digging things up is our trade.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:24.420
We're gonna form a plan.
I need all of your brains working!

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:33.720
Stulti, in orbit of planet N284,
is entering standby.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:40.350
Sorry, Alice, please stay
here just a bit longer.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:44.150
Clair, I leave Alice to you.

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.520
Roger Wilco!

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:46.900
What are those words?

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.990
It was written on a desk in the
school we used for briefing.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:57.740
You're slow!

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.320
Sorry...

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:02.770
Hurry up. The others are waiting.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:14.250
How about this, Ido?
Wanna part the way? I'll bet 2,000!

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.440
No thanks. The chances of winning
against an expert are zero.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:19.100
Heh, that's wise!

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:21.770
Stop spouting nonsense and
concentrate on the job.

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:24.400
I know, I know! Leave it to us.

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:29.570
Back then we had no idea how vast was the whirlpool of fate

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:36.600
that Ido and the rest of us
were dragged into.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:44.520
Prevention is better than cure, right?

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.890
Commander, may I have a word?

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:01.890
What is it?

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:07.210
Deploying a fleet just to expose some illegal
mining company makes way too little sense.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:09.860
Just what is the Earth side thinking?

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:11.570
Officer Watson.

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.240
Cast away your doubts.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:16.310
We should just follow orders.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:19.440
The tactical radar detected two I-Machines.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:21.080
Confirming ID codes.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:22.970
Code green, friendly.

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:25.020
One of them belongs to our army.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:26.540
What's its affiliation?

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:31.500
12th dispatched fleet's space regiment, 8th reconnaissance-in-force company commander,

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.560
first Lieutenant Amanza Volchkova.

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:35.670
She's bringing one of
the miners with her.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:38.390
A survivor from the heavily
damaged Marito...

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:39.550
Restrain them.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:46.230
She escaped from the mining ship?
That's a diversion for sure.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:48.510
Isn't that just fine?

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.750
Let's have the military dance for a bit.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.910
Drop your weapons.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:53.890
Me as well?

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.210
Drop them.

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:56.240
All right.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.500
Screw you, bitch! Dammit!

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:00.730
Don't move!

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:03.880
Damn it!

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:07.940
Lieutenant Amanza Volchkova, I presume?

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:09.060
Affirmative.

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:13.930
I took a hostage and escaped from the mining ship where I was held.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:16.170
I'll patch through the commander,
tell him directly.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:20.140
Lieutenant Amanza.
Tell me everything that happened.

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:22.350
Including the current position
of the illegal mining vessel.

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:27.020
Roger. Please let me use the
IFA channel for that.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.440
The dice are cast.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.890
It's in your hands, old man!

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:34.690
Starting to control the magnetic
field of the hull.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:37.030
And expanding the bumpers to max.

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:43.280
Clair! How long until the strongest flare?

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.700
Per Maya's estimation, in 15 minutes.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:50.790
These 20 shots are the last of our
Orichalt stock. Get ready, rascals!

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:53.080
All right, fly forth!

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:03.310
So when you escaped, the illegal mining ship was
in the Regulus System of the Leo Constellation?

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:04.050
Affirmative.

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:06.470
I'll have the Joint Fleet HQ confirm it.

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:10.400
You'll be under our supervision
until then. All right?

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.770
Do as you wish!

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:17.360
Rick!

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:18.610
Gotcha!

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:24.720
Lieutenant, my dear!

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:25.990
Don't be so familiar with me!

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.420
Amore, amore!

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:29.930
Do you want to die here?

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:30.960
Ah, I'm sorry.

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.250
It's almost time. Hurry up.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:35.670
Shut up, I know.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.560
Prominence in 32 seconds!

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.350
Yahoo!

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:51.000
This puts me on the wanted
list too, huh.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:56.980
It's time!

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.200
Arcade, confirmed.
Prominence has started!

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.660
Detected gravity waves from
the Orichalt missiles.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.290
The Orichalt warped!

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:22.260
Right! Let's, Miguel Jump, too!
Time to make our escape!

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:29.770
Directive ROE 03.
Scout 04, 05, give pursuit.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:32.100
Don't let them escape!
Take them out!

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.600
Detecting a gravity wave!

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.350
W-What?!

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:38.230
I-Machines for counter-attack!

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.110
Detecting plasma particles!

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:42.460
The Miguel Field...

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.990
Switch to emergency
defense protocols!

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.660
Tactical radars, down!

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.490
Engage the automatic shelter.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.160
Emergency steering!

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:55.080
For mere miners to destroy
a federation fleet!

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:57.910
Our job's done!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.210
It's your turn, Ido!

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:04.070
Prominence is estimated to last
for 530 more seconds.

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:08.030
But the fleet will probably
regroup earlier than that!

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:10.260
We'll do it in 450 seconds.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:13.810
Go, Fa-Loser!

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:26.500
Karla, can you do it?

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:30.490
Gotta pray that the federation's secret
protocols haven't changed.

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:35.240
Haven't changed?
You mean you've cracked them before?

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:37.970
For a fund manager, information is life.

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:41.250
Walking a tightrope this dangerous
is nothing special.

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:43.910
Though at some point I fell from one.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.010
Why did you do such a dangerous job?

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:47.920
I was conceited.

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:53.210
The authentication AI learning
progress has evolved.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:57.470
But the packet processing haven't changed.
I'll try attacking once again.

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:05.150
Abnormal access from the
data relay satellite A42?

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:09.390
It had an old authentication
AI because of budget issues.

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:13.530
Now I am certain they don't know anything.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.510
Administrator, open the door.

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:16.450
Affirmative.

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:22.000
Amazing, you got access!

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:26.170
Those idiots, the backdoor
I left is still there.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:27.930
Access complete!

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:31.060
Start from the highest secrecy levels
and only take what you can.

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:32.970
But even so, that's a huge amount...

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:36.720
Extract the data on the apparently
missing doctor Arisugawa.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:41.810
Most of the search results are
about Kain Arisugawa.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.970
Kain Arisugawa is the developer of the Mind Trance System,

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:48.420
CEO of the MT Laboratory, huh...

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.820
He's quite famous.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:52.250
There is almost no visual data.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:54.280
Well, he's famous for being eccentric.

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.620
But this is not the person
we're looking for.

00:18:56.620 --> 00:19:00.930
An astrophysicist going by
the name of Arisugawa...

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.290
There's no trace of him even
in the military secrets?

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.040
Was that ship's log faked?

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.100
It shouldn't be...

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:09.820
Ah!

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:10.970
Oh. What is it, Maya?

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:14.150
Take a look! It's a picture
of Kain Arisugawa!

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:15.430
He's...

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.720
Isn't it that guy the Observer, Sam?!

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:23.530
What does this mean?

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:26.530
The fleet will finish regrouping
in 30 seconds.

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:27.680
The data?

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:28.930
Just finished!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:30.360
Right, let's return!

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:34.570
That image looked like it was from
some kind of presentation...

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:35.910
I wonder what it was.

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:38.270
There's no use thinking about it now.

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:42.370
A gravity wave?

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:43.810
Here?

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:58.510
Ido? How did it go?

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.270
We've obtained the data, at least.

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:01.520
Where's Karla?

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:03.270
Sorry, I'm late.

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:07.380
Come on, we don't have time!
Let's skedaddle outta here!

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:09.440
You sound like a full-fledged criminal now.

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.200
So how did it go?

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:20.870
Just as planned.
However there's one uncertain thing.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.040
Excavator Ido.

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:26.120
He's reported to have no ID.

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:28.590
Could it be...

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:32.880
Clair, please search through the data
prioritizing the higher secrecy levels.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:34.090
Yeah, got it.

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:38.580
The only results for Arisugawa
are about Kain Arisugawa...

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:43.140
No data on Rajeev is coming out, either...
What's going on?

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:45.140
I mean, seriously?

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:48.220
Backdoor...

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:53.090
Was it left behind on purpose
to track our actions?

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:55.780
Just who has hidden all
of the important data?

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:58.170
Who was it?

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.080
Th-This is terrible!

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:02.990
What's wrong?

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:06.420
The data says that a wandering
planet appeared at Fifth!

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:08.670
It has a population of over
100 billion people!

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:09.840
What?!

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:13.340
Can you connect to an observation facility
nearby and give us a telescopic view?

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:14.630
This is Fifth!

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:18.740
There are many damage reports due to the giant wandering planet!

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.560
The colony is destroyed!

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:22.190
At this rate Fifth itself will...

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:06.910
I don't intend to cause any
further harm to you.

00:23:06.910 --> 00:23:09.290
What you're wishing for...

00:23:10.390 --> 00:23:11.520
It's this, isn't it?

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:13.660
Karla Milla-Foden.

00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:17.510
You can...
Return to being human.

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:21.520
My... body...

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:31.080
When the stone armor is eating the space,
everything will dissolve in sympathy.

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:36.190
Then, you who know something will
look in pity at the clueless fools.

00:23:36.190 --> 00:23:39.900
Where is the way a diseased spirit shall aim for?
